## Learn About Your Rights Irvine, Lemon Law Lawyers

Southern California is home to some of the heaviest traffic congestion in the country. To make matters worse, some are driving on these roads with defective vehicles that were not manufactured properly - also known as lemons.

Anyone can end up with a lemon, regardless of how reliable the seller is. Irvine, California lemon law - or the Song Beverly Consumer Warranty Act - was put in place to protect consumers if they purchased or leased a defective car.

As an Irvine lemon law lawyer, my mission is to help clients understand the lemon law process as we fight for the compensation they deserve.

The factors listed below may indicate you are entitled to benefits under Irvine, California lemon law.

- The vehicle manufacturer has made at least two or more attempts to repair a warranty-covered defect, or

- The vehicle has been out of service for more than 30 days while being repaired for warranty-covered problems; and

- The vehicle has several warranty-covered problems, which were not caused by abuse of the vehicle and that impair its use, value, or safety.

If you have a lemon on your hands - and the warranty is still in effect - there is a time limit to file a claim. You need an Irvine lemon law lawyer to do this as soon as possible.

The defect DOES NOT need to occur within the first 18 months after the purchase date or before 18,000 miles accrue on the odometer - a common misunderstanding. As long as the defect is reported within the terms of the warranty, your claim will be valid.

Once your vehicle is ruled a lemon, your Irvine lemon law lawyer will work to earn the following compensation:

Manufacturer coverage of your Irvine lemon law attorney and court costs.

A full refund of the vehicle’s original acquisition price plus incidental costs.

A replacement vehicle if necessary.

Earning justice for a lemon is not always easy. For consumers who don’t seek out professional aid, manufacturers will create a number of roadblocks - or deny your rights altogether.

